      "id": "T07-010",
      "verdict": "MUST",
      "status": "Native",
      "test": "the_prelude_carries_inhabited_and_nonempty",
      "why": "Inhabited (a Type 0 structure carrying data, with Inhabited_mk/Inhabited_default and the StructInfo that gates eta) and Nonempty (an indexed inductive at Prop with a checked constructor, so it cannot large-eliminate and choice stays an axiom) ARE now in the prelude. The case still fails on its last clause: resolve(Inhabited Nat) needs an add_instance, and Context::instances() is a push-only Vec resolved first-match, so a prelude entry would be entry zero and outrank every user instance. Measured cost of adding it: t02's instances().len() == 4 plus two elaborate resolution-order tests. Unblocks when a prelude instance can be a FALLBACK (lowest priority, or a keyed table) instead of a first match."
